# Supabase CLI local state. .temp/start-secrets holds a service-role key and a
# database URL for the local stack — never commit it. config.toml and any
# CLI-managed migrations can be added deliberately if the CLI is adopted; the
# schema currently lives in sql/migrations.
supabase/.branches
supabase/.temp

# Working documents, not source: the migration brief, the pre-overhaul
# baseline, and printed worklists. Worklists carry student names.
Document/
cohort-checkin-dossier.html

# tsc -b incremental build state (npm run typecheck)
*.tsbuildinfo

# A real attendance export lived here: 28 named students, their year group,
# their instructors and their absence counts. No code ever read it. Ignoring
# the whole of the repo root rather than one filename, because the next one
# will not be called attendance_report.csv — exports land here by default when
# somebody downloads one and forgets. Anything genuinely meant to be tracked
# can still be added with `git add -f`, or put somewhere other than the root.
/*.csv
